@startuml buffer-page-lifecycle
' ============================================================================
' Buffer-pool PAGE (frame) lifecycle — how one 256 KB block-storage page moves
' between disk and a buffer-pool frame, and through the Clean ⇄ Dirty and
' Pinned ⇄ Unpinned conditions that govern when it may be flushed or evicted.
'
' Source of truth: src/persistent_artrie/core/buffer_manager.rs
'   A `Frame` carries  block_id · lease_state (read-pin count | WRITE_LEASE) ·
'   dirty flag · reference_bit (CLOCK second-chance).  There is no literal
'   `enum PageState`; the lifecycle below is the product of
'     {resident, on-disk} × {clean, dirty} × {pinned, unpinned}.
'   Operations:  load_page / pin_page_data (fault-in) · pin_read / pin_write ·
'   unpin_read / unpin_write · mark_dirty (on write) · flush_page / flush_all
'   (write-back → clear_dirty) · get_free_frame (CLOCK victim eviction).
'   Invariants enforced by the code:
'     · a frame is NOT evictable while pinned (any read lease or the write lease);
'     · a dirty frame may NOT be flushed while a WRITE_LEASE is held;
'     · the CLOCK victim must be unpinned AND have reference_bit == 0;
'     · a dirty victim is written back (clear_dirty) before its frame is reused.
'
' Color key:
'   green (#C8E6C9) = page is RESIDENT in a buffer-pool frame (in memory)
'   amber (#FFE0B2) = transient control action (fault-in / write-back I/O)
'   blue  (#BBDEFB) = page lives only ON DISK (no resident frame)
'   grey  (#ECEFF1) = empty / free frame slot (infrastructure)
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
}

title Buffer-pool page (frame) lifecycle — fault-in · pin/unpin · dirty/flush · evict

state "On disk\n(no resident frame)" as Disk #BBDEFB : durable block in block-storage;\nthe SwizzledPtr child names it\nby block_id + location

state "Fault-in\nload_page / pin_page_data" as FaultIn #FFE0B2 : read_block_fixed(block_id)\ninto a free CLOCK frame,\nthen install in the page table

Disk -[#1565C0]-> FaultIn : access misses the buffer pool\n(page not in page_table)
FaultIn --> Resident : frame populated\n(reference_bit ← 1)

state "Resident in a buffer-pool frame" as Resident #C8E6C9 {

  state "Clean · Unpinned" as CleanUnpinned #C8E6C9 : dirty = false, lease_state = 0\n→ CLOCK-evictable
  state "Clean · Pinned" as CleanPinned #C8E6C9 : ≥1 read lease OR the write lease\n→ pinned, NOT evictable
  state "Dirty · Pinned" as DirtyPinned #C8E6C9 : modified under a lease\n(write differs from disk)
  state "Dirty · Unpinned" as DirtyUnpinned #C8E6C9 : modified, all leases dropped\n→ must be flushed before reuse

  [*] --> CleanUnpinned

  CleanUnpinned --> CleanPinned : pin_read / pin_write\n(lease acquired)
  CleanPinned --> CleanUnpinned : unpin_read / unpin_write\n(no writes performed)

  CleanPinned -[#C62828]-> DirtyPinned : mark_dirty\n(data_mut written under WRITE_LEASE)
  DirtyPinned --> DirtyUnpinned : unpin_write\n(lease released, still dirty)

  DirtyUnpinned --> CleanUnpinned : flush_page / flush_all\nwrite_block_fixed → clear_dirty
  DirtyPinned --> DirtyPinned : flush blocked\nwhile a WRITE_LEASE is held
}

' --- Reclaim: a clean, unpinned frame is taken as a CLOCK victim ---
Resident -[#1565C0]-> WriteBack : CLOCK victim is DIRTY\n(get_free_frame needs the frame)
state "Write-back\n(victim was dirty)" as WriteBack #FFE0B2 : write_block_fixed(old_block)\nthen clear_dirty
WriteBack -[#1565C0]-> Disk : frame detached\n(page_table entry removed)
CleanUnpinned -[#1565C0]-> Disk : CLOCK victim is CLEAN\n(reference_bit == 0) → frame reused as-is

note right of Resident #ECEFF1
  CLOCK (second-chance) reuse in get_free_frame:
  a frame is a candidate only when **unpinned**;
  a set reference_bit grants one reprieve (cleared,
  hand advances); a dirty victim is written back
  first so no acknowledged bytes are lost.
end note

legend right
| Color | Page condition |
|<#C8E6C9>| resident in a buffer-pool frame |
|<#FFE0B2>| fault-in / write-back I/O (transient) |
|<#BBDEFB>| on disk only (no resident frame) |
endlegend
@enduml
